title A Red player breaks away
intro Red has the ball in the middle of the field.
flip vertical

setup
  lineup 7v7
  player R-LF at 48, 28
  player B-CB at 46, 38
  player B-CM at 40, 50
  ball with R-LF

step
  caption You are the defender in blue. Watch what happens.
  label B-CB You

step
  caption Red runs at your goal. You track with them, but you are still beside them, not in front.
  R-LF to 32, 28
  B-CB to 33, 32
  ball with R-LF
  arrow from R-LF to 12, 30
  arrow from B-CB to 18, 34
  duration 1100

step
  caption Cut in front — get between Red and your goal.
  R-LF to 28, 28
  B-CB to 24, 29
  ball with R-LF
  arrow from R-LF to 12, 30
  arrow from B-CB to 18, 30
  duration 1100

question
  prompt Red is running at your goal and you are beside them. What should you do?
  answer Get between them and your goal
  wrong Chase them from behind
  wrong Keep running beside them
  wrong Sprint back to your goalie
  correct Get goal-side.
  why The quickest way to your goal is a straight line. Get onto that line first and Red has to go around you.

question
  prompt Why get between Red and your goal instead of running beside them?
  answer Red has to go around you
  wrong Red must pass backwards
  wrong You can catch them from behind
  wrong Red has to stop and wait
  correct Red has to go around you.
  why Standing in the way buys time. Every second you slow them down, another Blue player gets back to help.
